WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.490 --> 00:00:04.280
The CEO's sales dashboard takes 40 seconds to load.

2
00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:06.665
And it shows yesterday's numbers.

3
00:00:06.685 --> 00:00:11.015
Fix three things: the speed, the freshness, and who can see what.

4
00:00:11.035 --> 00:00:13.475
First: which tool shows the data?

5
00:00:13.495 --> 00:00:15.513
Looker Studio is free and quick.

6
00:00:15.533 --> 00:00:17.710
Great for simple dashboards.

7
00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:23.020
Looker adds a shared dictionary of metrics, so revenue means one thing for everyone.

8
00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:26.845
Connected Sheets lets spreadsheet people work on billions of rows,

9
00:00:26.865 --> 00:00:28.530
without an export.

10
00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:33.690
And BI Engine keeps data in memory, so dashboards answer in under a second.

11
00:00:33.710 --> 00:00:35.027
One classic trap.

12
00:00:35.047 --> 00:00:36.940
Looker Studio shows old data?

13
00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:38.102
It is the cache.

14
00:00:38.122 --> 00:00:40.915
Change the data freshness setting.

15
00:00:40.935 --> 00:00:44.000
Second: stop doing the same work again and again.

16
00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:46.612
A dashboard asks the same question all day.

17
00:00:46.632 --> 00:00:48.710
So work out the answer once.

18
00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:53.270
Use a materialized view, a scheduled summary table, or BI Engine.

19
00:00:53.290 --> 00:00:59.345
And the same query, asked twice, is served from the cache, free, for about 24 hours.

20
00:00:59.365 --> 00:01:01.145
Third: one query is still slow.

21
00:01:01.165 --> 00:01:02.355
Now what?

22
00:01:02.375 --> 00:01:03.105
Do not guess.

23
00:01:03.125 --> 00:01:04.455
Open the query plan.

24
00:01:04.475 --> 00:01:07.140
It shows bytes, slot time, and skew.

25
00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:09.377
Almost every fix is one of two things.

26
00:01:09.397 --> 00:01:11.700
Scan less, or shuffle less.

27
00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:13.612
Select only the columns you need.

28
00:01:13.632 --> 00:01:15.525
Filter on the partition early.

29
00:01:15.545 --> 00:01:17.960
And cut data down before a join.

30
00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:20.123
The trap: adding LIMIT to save money.

31
00:01:20.143 --> 00:01:23.285
BigQuery still scans every byte.

32
00:01:23.305 --> 00:01:25.920
Last: who can see what on the dashboard?

33
00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:28.545
Give viewers a view, or a curated dataset.

34
00:01:28.565 --> 00:01:30.380
Never the raw tables.

35
00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:33.155
And mask sensitive columns with policy tags.

36
00:01:33.175 --> 00:01:35.855
Share with groups, not people.

37
00:01:35.875 --> 00:01:37.115
Recap.

38
00:01:37.135 --> 00:01:39.040
Pick the BI tool for the audience.

39
00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:41.625
Compute once, and read many times.

40
00:01:41.645 --> 00:01:43.475
Read the plan, then scan less.

41
00:01:43.495 --> 00:01:46.285
And give viewers views, not raw tables.

42
00:01:46.305 --> 00:01:49.080
Try the checkpoint below.
